Yes, this is needed to let Roslyn know that it is unmanaged type with private fields.

If this field was deleted, the following would compile successfully:

```
SwiftIndirectResult M()
{
    SwiftIndirectResult x;
    return x;
}
```

With this field present, this will fail to compile with ` error CS0165: Use of unassigned local variable 'x'` error.
